      "solution": {
        "status": "ambiguous",
        "reasoning": "The base case is n=2, giving (3\\cdot2)!=720>8^2=64. Assume (3k)!>8^k for an arbitrary integer k\\ge2. The required next statement is (3(k+1))!>8^{k+1}. It follows because (3k+3)(3k+2)(3k+1)>8. For field-4, k>1 is also equivalent for integer k; k\\ge2 directly matches the stated domain. No captured answer or grade establishes Math Academy's key for this question; the worked example concerns a different inequality.",
