      "solution": {
        "status": "ambiguous",
        "reasoning": "The base case gives 2(3)^2=18>16. For k≥3, the inductive hypothesis yields 2(k+1)^2=2k^2+4k+2>(k+1)^2+4k+2>k^2+2+4k+2=(k+2)^2, where the second strict inequality follows from 2k−1>0. Induction therefore proves the statement for every natural number n≥3, so field-14 is option 1. Captured correct grades confirm fields 1–13, agreeing with the previous answers. Field-14 has no captured MA answer evidence yet.",
