      "solution": {
        "status": "ambiguous",
        "reasoning": "The base case n=2 gives 3^2=9=(2+1)^2. Assuming 3^k≥(k+1)^2 for k≥2 gives 3^{k+1}=3·3^k≥3(k+1)^2=(k+2)^2+2k^2+2k−1>(k+2)^2, since the remainder is at least 11. Thus induction establishes the statement for every natural number n≥2, so field-14 is option 1. Captured correct grades confirm fields 1–13; field-14 has no captured MA answer evidence.",
