      "solution": {
        "status": "ambiguous",
        "reasoning": "The base case is 2^{1-1}=1=1!. Assuming 2^{k-1}\\le k! for an integer k\\ge1, we obtain 2^k=2\\cdot2^{k-1}\\le2\\cdot k!\\le(k+1)\\cdot k!=(k+1)!, since k+1\\ge2. Induction therefore proves the statement for every integer n\\ge1. Fields 1–13 have captured correct grades. Field 14 requires the current option 2, n\\ge1; its selected value n=1 gives only the base case, not the full conclusion. No MA answer or grade for field 14 is captured, so its mathematical answer is certain but its source key remains unconfirmed. Entry failures supply no answer-key evidence.",
