      "question": {
        "dom_id": "step-q183431",
        "name": "Question 8",
        "problem": "Use mathematical induction to prove that ${3}^{n}\\ge (n+1)^{2}$ for $n\\ge 2,n\\in N.$\n\nWe proceed using induction on $n.$\n\n**Base Case**: We first prove that our statement is true for the base case $n=\\,${{field-1}}.\n\nFor the left-hand side, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{field-2}}={{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is\n{{field-4}}\nthe right-hand side.\nThus, our statement is {{field-5}} for $n=2.$",
        "worked_solution": "",
        "calculator_instructions": "",
