    "signature": "[\"question\", \"step-q183390:fields:field-14\", false, null, \"Use mathematical induction to prove that ${2}^{n-1}\\\\le n!$ for $n\\\\in N.$\\n\\nWe proceed using induction on $n.$\\n\\n**Base Case**: We first prove that our statement is true for the base case $n=\\\\,${{field-1}}.\\n\\nFor the left-hand side, we have\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}{{field-2}}={{field-3}}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nwhich is\\n{{field-4}}\\nthe right-hand side.\\nThus, our statement is {{field-5}} for $n=1.$\\n\\n**Inductive Hypothesis**: We assume that for some $n=$ {{field-6}}, we have\\n\\n$$\\n{{field-7}}\\\\le {{field-8}}.\\n$$\\n\\n**Inductive Step**: We have\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}{{field-9}} & ={{field-10}}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nand by the inductive hypothesis, \\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}2\\\\cdot {2}^{k-1} & \\\\le {{field-11}} \\\\\\\\  & \\\\le {{field-12}}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned} & ={{field-13}},\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nas required.\\n\\nTherefore, by the principle of induction, ${2}^{n-1}\\\\le n!$ is true for all\\n{{field-14}}.\", [], [[\"field-1\", false, [[\"k\", \"0\"], [\"0\", \"1\"], [\"1\", \"2\"]]], [\"field-2\", false, [[\"{2}^{0-1}\", \"0\"], [\"{2}^{2-1}\", \"1\"], [\"{2}^{1-1}\", \"2\"]]], [\"field-3\", false, [[\"4\", \"0\"], [\"1\", \"1\"], [\"2\", \"2\"]]], [\"field-4\", false, [[\"greater than\", \"0\"], [\"less than\", \"1\"], [\"equal to\", \"2\"]]], [\"field-5\", false, [[\"false\", \"0\"], [\"true\", \"1\"]]], [\"field-6\", false, [[\"k>2\", \"0\"], [\"k>3\", \"1\"], [\"k=3\", \"2\"], [\"k\\\\ge 1\", \"3\"]]], [\"field-7\", false, [[\"{2}^{k}\", \"0\"], [\"{2}^{k+1}\", \"1\"], [\"{2}^{k-1}\", \"2\"]]], [\"field-8\", false, [[\"(k-1)!\", \"0\"], [\"(k+1)!\", \"1\"], [\"k!\", \"2\"]]], [\"field-9\", false, [[\"{2}^{k-1}\", \"0\"], [\"{2}^{k}\", \"1\"], [\"{2}^{k+1}\", \"2\"]]], [\"field-10\", false, [[\"2\\\\cdot {2}^{k+1}\", \"0\"], [\"2\\\\cdot {2}^{k-1}\", \"1\"], [\"2\\\\cdot {2}^{k}\", \"2\"]]